incident_summary:
Notification by UDOT, a contractor ruptured a pressurized sewer line while boring.  
1000 West 1000 South Logan, Utah 
VAC trucks applied to release;
Flow is entering nearby pasture and ponding;
Quantity is unknown;
Called in Roto-Router for backup;
Locale is River Ranch area;
Location is ½ to 1 mile from Logan River;
Logan City and Bear River Health are involved;
Logan City walked the perimeter of the pasture and estimate it’s size at 10 acres;
Release is contained to the pasture field;
Fourteen inch line has been shut off;
Flow is received into pump station from Providence and East Logan;
This is a main trunk feeding this lift-station;
Zone of cat-tails and bulrush between pasture and Logan River;
Potential to back-up and flood resident homes if flow is allowed to build;
Logan City is requesting permission to run pump(s) sending flow to pasture to prevent flooding homes;
Bear River recommends constant monitoring and surveillance on zone of impact to pasture;
Authorities can review afterward to determine if additional ground/soil treatment is required;
Pasture and flow from it does not present an immediate threat to waters of the state.

